{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Sykes&limit=10&title=The Seven Daughters of Eve","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"seven daughters of Eve"},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Sykes, Bryan","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"W.W. Norton & Co.","dateIssued":"2001","edition":"1st American ed.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"x, 306 p. ; 25 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"From Eve, the earliest known hominid, discovered in Africa, geneticist Sykes traces a genetic linkage to 7 prehistoric European women. Sykes conveys the excitement and drama of his discovery of strands of DNA that passed unbroken through the maternal line. He names the 7 women he found in that line and extrapolates probable lives for them."},"tableOfContents":"Iceman's relative found in Dorset -- So, what is DNA and what does it do? -- From blood groups to genes -- Special messenger -- Tsar and I -- Puzzle of the Pacific -- Greatest voyagers -- First Europeans -- Last of the Neanderthals -- Hunters and farmers -- We are not amused -- Cheddar man speaks -- Adam joins the party -- Seven daughters -- Ursula -- Xenia -- Helena -- Velda -- Tara -- Katrine -- Jasmine -- World -- Sense of self.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Bryan Sykes."},"Includes index.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Ev